# Heartbeats - BehalfBot-open template

**This file is a template.** The dispatcher does NOT read it. Copy it to `HEARTBEATS.md` (gitignored, per-install) and register your heartbeats there:

```bash
cp HEARTBEATS.md.template HEARTBEATS.md
```

Declarative work queue for the heartbeat dispatcher (`scheduled-tasks/heartbeat-dispatcher.sh`). Each `##` section defines a heartbeat: when to check, how to gather data, when to fire the model.

> Lessons carried over from the chassis:
>
> - Scaffolding a heartbeat (script + prompt + state file) without registering it here means the dispatcher never invokes it. Silent dormancy. **Register every new heartbeat in this file in the same PR as the supporting scripts.**
> - The gather script is the right place for expensive checks to no-op cheaply. Every dispatcher tick (~96/day on the default 15-min cadence) is fine IF the gather short-circuits on trivial conditions before any paid API call.
> - Validate this file's YAML blocks with `bash scripts/validate-heartbeats.sh` before commit. A malformed block silently disables the heartbeat without erroring.

---

## Heartbeat schema

Each heartbeat is one `##` heading + a fenced ` ```yaml ` block. The dispatcher parser uses these fields:

| Field | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `schedule` | yes | When to check. Formats: `every 15m`, `every 1h`, `daily 08:00`, `weekly sunday 18:00`, or `disabled` to park it |
| `gather` | yes | Path (relative to the repo root) to a shell script that emits JSON on stdout. Either `{"count": N}` for threshold conditions, or any structured JSON for `ask_model` / `always` |
| `condition` | yes | One of: `always`, `threshold <field> <op> <value>` (e.g. `threshold count > 0`), `ask_model` (requires Ollama) |
| `prompt` | yes | Path (relative to the repo root) to a markdown file the model reads on fire |
| `model` | yes | A `venice/<model>` string (e.g. `venice/zai-org-glm-5-2`) or a chassis alias: `opus`, `sonnet`, `haiku` (mapped via `HEARTBEAT_MODEL_*` env vars) |
| `budget` | yes | Advisory max USD per invocation. OpenCode has no hard budget cap; the dispatcher logs a WARN when the summed run cost exceeds this |
| `criticality` | yes | `critical` (runs in conservation mode), `normal`, `background` |
| `cwd` | no | Working directory for the run (passed as `opencode run --dir`). Defaults to the repo root |
| `output_validator` | no | `true` to run the Five Failure Modes small-model check on the output |
| `max_fires_per_day` | no | Daily ceiling on model runs for this heartbeat. Defaults to `DISPATCHER_DEFAULT_MAX_FIRES_PER_DAY` (24 in compose). Absolute until the date rolls |
| `max_usd_per_day` | no | Daily spend ceiling for this heartbeat, from the dispatcher's telemetry. All heartbeats together are also capped by `DISPATCHER_MAX_USD_PER_DAY` (docs/control.md) |
| `condition_prompt` | no | Required when condition=ask_model. Question to send to Ollama |
| `jitter` | no | Random offset added to daily schedules (e.g. `30m`, `1h`). Deterministic per day+name |

